1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,680
you're paying for AI capability.

2
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:04,800
But the real skill is knowing when to use

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,040
which level of capability.

4
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:08,240
Claude is not just one model.

5
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:09,720
It gives you a set of models

6
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:11,460
and each one has a different job.

7
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:13,140
Let's look at the model lineup.

8
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:14,200
Start with Sonnet.

9
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:16,660
Claude Sonnet 5 is now the default model

10
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:17,700
for free and pro users.

11
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:20,300
It is also the model most people should use

12
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:21,260
most of the time.

13
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:22,980
Anthropic describes it

14
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:25,240
as the most agentic Sonnet model yet.

15
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:27,220
That means it is better at planning,

16
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:28,360
using tools,

17
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:30,880
following through on multi-step tasks

18
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:33,060
and handling everyday knowledge work.

19
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:35,060
Think drafting, summarizing,

20
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:36,120
research synthesis,

21
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:37,380
artifact review,

22
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:39,720
coding and workflow automation.

23
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:41,920
For most leadership tasks,

24
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:43,960
Sonnet is the right starting point.

25
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:46,320
It gives you a strong balance of speed,

26
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:47,900
quality and cost.

27
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:50,520
Then there is Haiku, the lightweight model.

28
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:54,020
Use Haiku when speed matters more than depth.

29
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:55,820
It is useful for quick summaries,

30
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:58,400
simple rewrites, classification, routing

31
00:00:58,400 --> 00:00:59,860
or high volume tasks

32
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:01,700
where you do not need deep reasoning.

33
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:03,420
Then there is Opus.

34
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:06,780
Opus 4.8 is the deeper reasoning model.

35
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:08,900
Use it when the work is harder,

36
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:10,840
messier or higher stakes.

37
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:13,220
For example, a strategic decision,

38
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:15,140
a complex financial analysis,

39
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:16,760
a sensitive executive message

40
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:18,880
or a task where the first answer

41
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:21,080
needs to be more complete and considered.

42
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:23,700
You do not need Opus for everything.

43
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:26,300
Think of it as the specialist you bring in

44
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:28,300
when Sonnet's first pass is not enough.

45
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:30,320
Finally, there is Fable.

46
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:33,780
Fable 5 is Anthropics' most powerful model.

47
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:35,780
It was recently released more broadly

48
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:37,600
after being paused for safety updates.

49
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:40,000
It is built for hard thinking tasks

50
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,320
and for AI systems that can plan

51
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:44,560
and carry out many steps over time.

52
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:47,120
For example, it can research a topic,

53
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:49,260
create a plan, write documents,

54
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:50,980
improve them based on feedback

55
00:01:50,980 --> 00:01:53,180
and manage tasks across tools

56
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:54,400
with little human help.

57
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:57,320
However, as the most capable model,

58
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,920
Fable 5 will draw down your usage

59
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:02,160
much faster than Opus 4.8.

60
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:04,260
So it is best suited for teams

61
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:06,200
building serious AI systems

62
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,840
rather than most daily individual tasks.

63
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:12,600
Now, where do you find and switch these models?

64
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:14,920
To switch models, start a new chat

65
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:16,260
and click the model name

66
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:18,180
in the right corner of the prompt box.

67
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:20,080
That opens the model picker

68
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:22,040
where you'll see your available options.

69
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:24,520
You'll also notice the effort options

70
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:26,100
from the model selection dropdown.

71
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:28,780
This lets you decide how much effort

72
00:02:28,780 --> 00:02:30,340
Claude should put into a response.

73
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:32,740
Keep in mind, the higher the effort,

74
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:33,740
the slower the response

75
00:02:33,740 --> 00:02:35,300
and the faster the credits run out.

76
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:36,600
So how should you choose?

77
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:40,040
Use Haiku when the task is simple and speed matters.

78
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:42,720
Use Sonnet for most daily work,

79
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:45,700
drafting, planning, summarizing, analysis,

80
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:47,700
coding and working with documents.

81
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:51,160
Use Opus when the task needs deeper judgment

82
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:52,620
or a stronger first pass.

83
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:55,800
Use Fable when you are building with the API,

84
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:57,740
working with very long context

85
00:02:57,740 --> 00:03:00,780
or designing a long running agentic workflow.

86
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:04,100
Now, a quick note on availability and pricing.

87
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:07,320
Claude Sonetti 5 is available across all plans

88
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:09,380
and is the default for free in Pro.

89
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:12,040
Claude Opus 4.8 is available on Pro,

90
00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:13,820
Macs, Team and Enterprise.

91
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:16,280
On Pro, usage is capped

92
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:18,180
because Opus costs more compute.

93
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:21,180
If you hit that limit, move to Macs for higher usage.

94
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:24,060
Claude Fable 5 is not on the free tier.

95
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:26,100
It is available on paid plans

96
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:28,820
and strictly limited to up to 50%

97
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:30,180
of your weekly usage limits.

98
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:32,360
So keep in mind, the model you pick

99
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:34,600
shapes the result before you write a single word.

100
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,440
Start making that distinction today

101
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:38,440
and you'll get more out of Claude.
